---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import portrait from "../assets/aaron-saray.jpg";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const title = "Who am I";
const description = "And now you'll know... the rest of the story.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <main id="main" class="page-column">
    <div class="flex items-start gap-5 sm:items-end sm:gap-7">
      <Image
        src={portrait}
        alt="Aaron Saray"
        width={96}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
        class="block aspect-square h-auto w-20 shrink-0 object-cover sm:w-24"
      />
      <div class="min-w-0">
        {
          /* The row aligns the portrait to this block's edges, so both ends
            are trimmed to the letters: the heading's leading above the cap
            height here, the lede's below the last baseline. Untrimmed, the
            line box leaves ~7px of half-leading and descender space the eye
            reads as the portrait sitting too low. */
        }
        <h1 class="page-title [text-box:trim-start_cap_alphabetic]">
          Aaron Saray
        </h1>
        <p
          class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink [text-box:trim-end_cap_alphabetic]"
        >
          Pronounced suh-RAY. Google says there is only one of me... and it
          looks like you found me, too. Hello 👋
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink sm:mt-12">
      <p>
        I live in Milwaukee - and other parts of Wisconsin, depending on the
        year, the weather, the traffic or the wifi.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm trying my best - whether it's still learning Spanish, or working to
        limit my <s>fucking</s> potty mouth.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 sm:mt-16">
      <h2 class="section-title">Where I'm From</h2>
      <div class="prose mt-5">
        <p>
          It wasn't that hard to keep 8-year-old Aaron happy. All it took was a
          Commodore 64/VIC-20, a Black and White TV, the manual, and a few 3-2-1
          Contact magazines. The northwoods of Wisconsin didn't have dependable
          electricity, and I wasn't a rich kid who could afford the luxuries of
          a printer or a tape drive (the computer was a hand-me-down and the TV
          was rescued from a dumpster). When the power blinked, I lost all of my
          work. That's how I learned to type really fast. Not much has changed
          these days - except now we have multiple terabyte hard drives and I've
          invested quite disproportionately in UPSs.
        </p>
        <p>
          The patience, well, that was another story. My first technical job was
          at an internet service provider, doing tech support. While I later got
          promoted to the web development team, it was those initial years that
          taught me patience, understanding and converting technical things for
          a non-technical audience.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 sm:mt-16">
      <h2 class="section-title">How I Work</h2>
      <div class="prose mt-5">
        <p>
          <b class="font-medium text-ink">I want to know everything.</b> Tell me all
          of the facts, concerns, past successes and failures, current restrictions
          and future risks. The more information the better. And no, I'm not one of
          those jackasses that just try to sell you on the most expensive service
          or the thing that's easiest for me. With the full picture, I'll tell you
          how I best fit in - or if I would suggest working with someone else.
        </p>
        <p>
          <b class="font-medium text-ink">
            Making things better is about understanding the world is grey.
          </b>
          The middle ground is where businesses make money. We can't throw everything
          away and rewrite it. But it just can't stay like this either.
        </p>
        <p>
          <b class="font-medium text-ink">
            The part of me that can't leave it like that - that's the same part
            of me that is furious when a bug (or missed requirement) is mine.
          </b>
          Don't let my measured approach fool you; internally, I'm fuming.
        </p>
        <p>
          <b class="font-medium text-ink">Don't be wrong.</b> But when you are, accept
          the facts, apologize and move on. I like being given a fact I didn't have
          before. It means I get to learn something new.
        </p>
        <p>
          <b class="font-medium text-ink">
            And yes, I still read those manuals.
          </b>
          If only because I like to know if AI is lying to me.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 sm:mt-16">
      <h2 class="section-title">Now What?</h2>
      <dl class="prose mt-5">
        <div>
          <dt class="font-medium text-ink"><a href="/blog/">My blog</a></dt>
          <dd class="mt-1">
            700+ entries over 2 decades. There's a little bit for everyone,
            whether you're interested in <a href="/tag/management/"
              >management</a
            > or <a href="/tag/laravel/">Laravel</a>, <a href="/tag/business/"
              >business</a
            >, or just random <a href="/tag/iot/">home automation</a>.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-medium text-ink"><a href="/cv/">My CV</a></dt>
          <dd class="mt-1">
            but how do you know I even know what I'm talking about? Check out
            what I've been doing for the last little bit. Work experience, open
            source, volunteering.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-medium text-ink">
            <a href="https://masteringlaravel.io">Mastering Laravel</a>
          </dt>
          <dd class="mt-1">
            Whether you're into Laravel articles and books - or you're more a
            podcast sort of person - I've been teaching and talking about
            Laravel for a while now. Get your fill.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-medium text-ink"><a href="/contact/">Contact</a></dt>
          <dd class="mt-1">
            Are we about to become best friends? Really?! Either way, you
            probably have some questions, or want me to help you out. Let's
            chat.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
